{"id":17774,"name":"Mobile County","slug":"mobile-county","state":"Alabama","code":"AL","program":null,"sourceUrl":"https://vault.taxlienschool.com/tax-lien/tax-lien-states/alabama-tax-lien-sales-how-to-get-12-interest/mobile-county/","lastUpdated":"2026-07-13T12:29:23","facts":{"taxSaleType":"Tax Lien Sale","bidProcedure":"Bid Down","redemptionPeriod":"3 years generally before you can foreclose","interestRate":"12%","extra":[{"label":"Typical Date of Sale","value":"May"},{"label":"Auction Site","value":"GovEase"},{"label":"County Website","value":"Mobile County Revenue Commissioner"},{"label":"Property Search","value":"Mobile County Property Search"}]},"bodyHtml":"\n<figure class=\"wp-block-embed is-type-video is-provider-youtube wp-block-embed-youtube wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"><div class=\"wp-block-embed__wrapper\">\n<span class=\"PTCRrzYz4FkYUGpEa30myZhsM1qGwH2vjVPd4I5EiTvOwxSoLbprWA99lNN5dgkFXnZ2J83SoLUDKtyWM16blfee7nDhxctI7Qs\"><iframe title=\"Could You Secure a 12% ROI? - Mobile County - Alabama Tax Lien Investing\" width=\"1170\" height=\"658\" src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/SMR7jG5vkwM?feature=oembed\" frameborder=\"0\" allow=\"accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share\" referrerpolicy=\"strict-origin-when-cross-origin\" allowfullscreen></iframe></span>\n</div></figure>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-buttons is-content-justification-center is-layout-flex wp-container-core-buttons-is-layout-16018d1d wp-block-buttons-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-button\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link wp-element-button\" href=\"https://linktr.ee/dustinhahnrealestateinvesting\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Click Here to Get Dustin Hahn’s Tax Lien and Deed FREE Mini-Course</a></div>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<div style=\"height:30px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"Could-You-Secure-a-12%-ROI?---Mobile-County---Alabama-Tax-Lien-Investing\">Could You Secure a 12% ROI? &#8211; Mobile County &#8211; Alabama Tax Lien Investing</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>Are you looking to invest with the possibility of a 12% return? Mobile County, Alabama&#8217;s Tax Lien Auction every May is your shot, available online at <a href=\"https://govease.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-vivid-cyan-blue-color\">GovEase</mark></a>: Online Real Estate Auction for Tax Liens &amp; Tax Deed Sales.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>This isn&#8217;t about grabbing property; it&#8217;s about securing a lien against it due to unpaid taxes and then earning interest. Here’s a guide to get you started:</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Mobile County Tax Lien Auction Details</h3>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"></figure>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Auction Participation</h3>\n\n\n\n<p>To participate, you&#8217;ll need to register on <a href=\"https://govease.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-vivid-cyan-blue-color\">GovEase</mark></a>: Online Real Estate Auction for Tax Liens &amp; Tax Deed Sales and make a 10% deposit of your bid amount. Payments are accepted via ACH, debit/credit card, or wire transfer. Bidding focuses on the interest rate you&#8217;re willing to accept, starting from 12% and potentially dropping to 0%. If there&#8217;s a tie at 0%, a random draw decides the winner​​.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Bidding Process</h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Pre-bidding</strong>: Available from May 11 and 12, 2024.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Live Auction</strong>: Each tax lien offered will be open for bidding for 30 seconds. If a bid is placed in the last 10 seconds, the clock resets for an additional 10 seconds​​.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Post-Auction Details</h3>\n\n\n\n<p>After the auction, winning bidders get a report listing their parcels and amounts due. Property owners have the option to redeem their lien by covering the tax debt plus your interest rate​.</p>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<figure class=\"aligncenter size-full\"><picture><source srcset=\"https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Mobile-County-Alabama-USA-Skyline.webp 1081w,https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Mobile-County-Alabama-USA-Skyline-541x360.webp 541w,https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Mobile-County-Alabama-USA-Skyline-296x197.webp 296w,https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Mobile-County-Alabama-USA-Skyline-768x512.webp 768w,https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Mobile-County-Alabama-USA-Skyline-20x13.webp 20w,https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Mobile-County-Alabama-USA-Skyline-32x21.webp 32w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1081px) 100vw, 1081px\" type=\"image/webp\"><img src=\"https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Mobile-County-Alabama-USA-Skyline.png\" height=\"720\" width=\"1081\" srcset=\"https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Mobile-County-Alabama-USA-Skyline.png 1081w, https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Mobile-County-Alabama-USA-Skyline-541x360.png 541w, https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Mobile-County-Alabama-USA-Skyline-296x197.png 296w, https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Mobile-County-Alabama-USA-Skyline-768x512.png 768w, https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Mobile-County-Alabama-USA-Skyline-20x13.png 20w, https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Mobile-County-Alabama-USA-Skyline-32x21.png 32w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1081px) 100vw, 1081px\" class=\"wp-image-17777 sp-no-webp\" alt=\"Mobile County Alabama USA Skyline\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"  > </picture></figure>\n</div>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-buttons is-content-justification-center is-layout-flex wp-container-core-buttons-is-layout-16018d1d wp-block-buttons-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-button is-style-outline is-style-outline--1\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link wp-element-button\" href=\"https://linktr.ee/dustinhahnrealestateinvesting\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Click Here to Book a Call with Dustin Hahn</a></div>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<div style=\"height:30px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Research and Due Diligence</h3>\n\n\n\n<p>It’s crucial to research these properties to assess their worth and any attached obligations. Use the Mobile County Property Search tool to look up parcel information by the owner, address, key number, or parcel ID​​.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Interesting Facts about Mobile County Real Estate</h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Auction Advertisement</strong>: The Call News and the Mobile County Revenue Commissioner&#8217;s Website advertise the auction.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Encumbrances</strong>: The sale of a tax lien does not extinguish any deed restriction, deed covenant, or easement on the property​​.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"FAQs-for-Tax-Lien-Investing\">FAQs for Tax Lien Investing</h3>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Q: What happens if the property owner redeems the lien?</strong><br>A: The property owner can redeem their property by paying the overdue taxes plus the interest rate you bid. You’ll receive this payment as a return on your investment.</p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Q: Can I participate in the auction without attending in person?</strong><br>A: Yes, they conduct the auction online via GovEase. You must have a computer with internet access and a web browser​​.</p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Q: What if I win a bid at 0% interest?</strong><br>A: A random number generator chooses the winner when multiple bidders tie at 0%​​.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>For more detailed information, visit the Mobile County Revenue Commissioner&#8217;s FAQ page.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Useful Links</h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><a href=\"https://mobilecopropertytax.com/taxliensale/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-vivid-cyan-blue-color\">Mobile County Tax Lien Sale Info</mark></a></li>\n\n\n\n<li><a href=\"https://mobilecopropertytax.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-vivid-cyan-blue-color\">Revenue Commissioner Website</mark></a></li>\n\n\n\n<li><a href=\"https://www.mobilecountyal.gov/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-vivid-cyan-blue-color\">Mobile County Official Site</mark></a></li>\n\n\n\n<li><a href=\"https://vault.taxlienschool.com/tax-lien/tax-lien-states/alabama-tax-lien-sales-how-to-get-12-interest/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-vivid-cyan-blue-color\">How to Earn up to 12% Interest from Alabama&#8217;s Tax Lien Sales</mark></a></li>\n\n\n\n<li><a href=\"https://vault.taxlienschool.com/tax-lien/tax-lien-investing-overview/understanding-tax-lien-certificates/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-vivid-cyan-blue-color\">Learn How Does Tax Lien Investing Work</mark></a></li>\n\n\n\n<li><a href=\"https://youtu.be/eNKIUQC6io0?si=b31MOzg-xCeQzAUA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-vivid-cyan-blue-color\">Want to get started with Tax Liens? Click Here!</mark></a></li>\n\n\n\n<li><a href=\"htt